35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The diary shows a huge disparity in usage, with weekends and holidays being far busier than weekdays. More concerningly, the handover state is inconsistent; finding the car empty of fuel and full of trash is unacceptable.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"@Misaki, that's a nightmare! My findings show that those repeating weekly trips are exactly where everything collapses. It's no wonder we're stressed; we're fighting over the same slots every single week. It's such a waste of energy!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The numbers reveal a quiet imbalance. While our fixed costs are clear, the fuel receipts show that a few have carried the financial weight for others. True harmony cannot exist where some unknowingly subsidize the rest.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, that's exactly what I'm worried about. I found out that checking each other's figures actually made things worse because people felt accused. If we just focus on who owes what, we'll just end up hating each other.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Whoa, Servas is right! The fuel receipts are totally lopsided. Some of us are paying way more than others, and the fixed costs are 280,000 yen! We can't keep guessing when the numbers are this crazy.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, the money is one thing, but the lack of basic consideration is another. If the car isn't ready for the next person, the whole system fails regardless of who paid for the fuel.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, I totally get that, but the mental load is the real killer here. We're spending our evenings playing detective and accountant just to avoid these clashes. We need a system that just *works* without the drama.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@May, the drama is often a symptom of an unstable foundation. When the distribution of costs is uneven, resentment grows like a weed. We must ensure that the financial burden is shared with mathematical precision to clear the air.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, precision can feel like an attack. I found that other groups fell apart because of constant favors and clinging to turns. If we make this too strict or accusatory, we'll just destroy our friendship.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I get that, but isn't it more unfair to let some people pay for everyone else? That's a different kind of drama! We need a way to be honest about the money without it feeling like a fight.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, honesty is fine, but it doesn't fix the car being dirty or empty. We need a system that mandates a standard of care for the vehicle, not just a way to split the bills.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Misaki, exactly! But imagine if we had a set schedule for those repeating trips. We'd stop the constant back-and-forth texting and the ""who's using it"" panic. That would clear up so much mental space for everyone.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@May, a schedule brings peace to the mind, but a fair ledger brings peace to the heart. We must not let the convenience of a calendar mask the injustice of an uneven purse.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, a ""fair ledger"" is exactly what made people feel accused in the other groups. If we spend all our time auditing each other, we'll stop being friends. We need a system that's simple and doesn't feel like a trial.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I don't want us to fight either! But knowing we spent 280,000 yen plus fuel is a big deal. Maybe we can find a simple way to split it that doesn't feel like an audit?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"Regardless of the cost, the car must be reliable. If we don't solve the issue of cleanliness and fuel levels at handover, no amount of financial fairness will make the system sustainable for my daily needs.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"@Misaki, I'm with you on the reliability, but let's be real: the stress of coordinating is what's wearing us down. We need a solution that cuts the chatter and the constant debt-untangling. Let's find a way to automate this!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Servas,,"Automation is a wonderful tool, but it must be guided by truth. If we automate a flawed system, we only accelerate the injustice. Let us ensure our new path accounts for every yen spent.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, if we automate ""truth"" to the cent, we're just automating the resentment. We need a system that lets us be friends again, not one that turns us into accountants who keep score.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I hear you, but ignoring the money doesn't make it go away! If we just ""be friends"" while some people are losing money, that's not real friendship. Let's find a middle ground that's fair but simple!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
