60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option A seems the most reliable. If I have my own designated days, I can trust the car will be there for my routine without the stress of a booking war or constant coordination.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"@Misaki, I'm totally with you! Option A is a dream because it kills the coordination nightmare. No more endless texting or untangling debts every single night—just a fixed day and a fixed price. Simple!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Servas,,"While simplicity is a virtue, Option A risks continuing the quiet subsidies we discovered. A fixed share ignores the reality of who actually drives. Option C, though more complex, ensures that costs follow usage with mathematical fairness.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, Option C is exactly what I'm afraid of. Recording every distance and dividing costs by the kilometer is just ""checking figures"" again. It'll turn us back into accountants and start the accusations all over.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I see your point, but Option A feels like we're just guessing again! If some of us barely drive, why pay the same? Option C is fair, but maybe it's too much work?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, the ""work"" of Option C is exactly what leads to the friction Takumi mentioned. More importantly, Option C doesn't guarantee the car is ready for me on a Tuesday morning; it just tracks the cost.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, exactly! Option C is just more bookkeeping and more ""who owes what"" drama. Option A is the only one that actually gives us our free time back. Let's just pick the one that stops the headaches!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@May, peace of mind is precious, but it should not be bought with the silence of the burdened. If we choose Option A, we simply hide the imbalance. True harmony requires an honest accounting of our shared life.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, hiding the imbalance is better than fighting over every single yen. Option A stops the ""favors"" and the ""clinging to turns"" that ruin groups. It lets us stop talking about the car and start being friends again.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I really want us to be friends, but it's hard to be happy knowing some of us are paying for others. Still, Option C sounds like a lot of work. Maybe Option A is the best compromise?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, it is the best compromise. It provides the stability I need for my routine and removes the friction of constant auditing. If we agree on a standard of care, Option A is the most sustainable.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,"@Misaki, exactly! Let's just agree on the cleaning rules and call it a day. Option A is the only way to stop the mental drain of coordinating everything. I'm voting for A to save my sanity!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@May, sanity is a fragile thing when built upon a foundation of inequality. I cannot in good conscience vote for a system that allows some to quietly subsidize others. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, your ""truth"" is what makes people feel accused. I'm voting for Option A. It's the only way to stop the constant score-keeping and actually protect our friendship before it's too late.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, I really wanted the truth, but @Takumi is right about the fighting. If Option C makes us act like accountants, it's not worth it. I'll vote for Option A to keep us all friends!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. Option A provides the predictability I need for my midweek routine and removes the constant friction. As long as we commit to keeping the car clean and fueled, it is the most practical choice. I vote for A.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,"I'm so glad we're on the same page! No more detective work, no more endless spreadsheets, and finally, some peace and quiet in our group chat. I'm voting for Option A!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is a heavy heart that accepts a compromise of fairness for the sake of peace. However, I see that the spirit of this group yearns for simplicity over precision. I remain with Option C.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Takumi,,I'm voting for Option A. It's the only way to stop the fighting and the feeling of being accused. Let's choose our friendship over a perfect ledger and just move forward together.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm voting for Option A too! Even though I love the real numbers, I love you guys more. Let's just be fair with the cleaning and keep things simple. Option A it is!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
